
.TH SIMPLE_SHELL 1 "April 2026" "simple_shell" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
simple_shell \- simple UNIX command interpreter

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B simple_shell

.SH DESCRIPTION
simple_shell is a simple command-line interpreter that mimics basic
features of a Unix shell.

It reads commands from standard input and executes them. The shell
supports execution of programs with arguments using the PATH environment
variable.

This shell is not intended to be a full implementation of a standard
Unix shell and does not support all advanced features.

.SH FEATURES
.TP
.B Command execution
Executes external commands found in the PATH
.TP
.B Built-in commands
Supports basic built-ins such as cd, exit, and env
.TP
.B Prompt
Displays a prompt and waits for user input
.TP
.B End of file
Handles Ctrl+D to exit the shell

.SH BUILTIN COMMANDS
.TP
.B cd
Change the current working directory
.TP
.B exit
Exit the shell
.TP
.B env
Display the current environment variables

.SH EXAMPLES
Execute a command:
.PP
ls -l
.PP
Change directory:
.PP
cd /tmp

.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns 0 on success, or a non-zero value on error.

.SH LIMITATIONS
This shell does not support:
- pipes (|)
- logical operators (&&, ||)
- command separators (;)
- wildcard expansion (*)

